{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01TpwfPcWi8NTd9xidCV2CMX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me start implementing the leave-web-app. I'll create the following files:\n\n1. `package.json`\n2. `tsconfig.json`\n3. `vite.config.ts`\n4. `index.html`\n5. `src/main.tsx`\n6. `src/App.tsx`\n7. `src/api.ts`\n8. `src/context/UserContext.tsx`\n9. `src/types/index.ts`\n10. `src/components/` - various components\n\n\n11. `src/pages/` - Employee and Manager views\n12. `nginx.conf`\n13. `entrypoint.sh`\n14. `Dockerfile`\n15. `workload.yaml`\n\nI need to plan out the API endpoints I'll be consuming—health checks, leave types, employee balances, and the full lifecycle of leave requests including approvals and rejections. For the MVP, I'll hardcode the user context to store role and ID.\n\nI'm going back and forth on the styling approach. Tailwind CSS with Vite is straightforward and clean, though I considered Material-UI for its pre-built components like date pickers and tables. Plain CSS would be simpler but less polished. I'll go with Tailwind since it strikes the right balance for this project.\n\nSetting up the project structure...\n\nI need to handle the API base URL carefully for the SPA pattern - either using a runtime-injected window variable, Vite environment variables, or defaulting to localhost for development.\n\nThe nginx configuration will proxy `/api/` requests to the `LEAVE_SERVICE_URL` backend service, and I'll use port 3000 as specified in the requirements.\n\nNow I'm setting up all the project files with React 18, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS, and necessary libraries like React Router for navigation, react-hot-toast for notifications, and react-datepicker for the leave request date selection.\n\nI need to create the TypeScript types, set up the UserContext to manage role and employee ID state, build the LoginPage for role selection, and then create the EmployeePage with the leave request form and balance display, plus the ManagerPage for handling pending requests with approve/reject functionality.\n\nFor the API communication, the app will use `/api` as the base URL since nginx will proxy those requests to the actual backend service URL injected at runtime through the `env.js` file.\n\nNow I'm realizing there's a potential mismatch with the API paths—the backend endpoints already include `/api` in their routes, so I need to verify whether the base URL should actually be empty or if the backend service is structured differently than I initially thought. at the API spec from the leave-service issue to understand. Based on the paths in the OpenAPI spec for the frontend:\n- GET /api/leave-types\n- GET /api/employees/{employeeId}/balance\n- POST /api/leave-requests\n- etc.\n\nIf the backend service serves these routes at `/api/...`, then when nginx proxies `/api/leave-types` to `LEAVE_SERVICE_URL/leave-types`, that would strip the `/api` prefix. \n\nThe nginx proxy_pass with a trailing slash strips the location prefix, so a request to `/api/leave-types` gets proxied to `LEAVE_SERVICE_URL/leave-types`. This only works if the backend's actual routes are at `/leave-types` rather than `/api/leave-types`.\n\nSince I don't know the leave-service internals, I need to infer from the API spec. The frontend's OpenAPI spec lists endpoints like `/api/leave-types`, `/api/employees/{employeeId}/balance`, and `/api/leave-requests`, which suggests the backend likely serves these at the root level without the `/api` prefix, making the nginx stripping behavior correct. a request to `/api/foo` becomes `LEAVE_SERVICE_URL/foo` with the `/api/` prefix stripped. I'll use `LEAVE_SERVICE_URL` as the environment variable name per the issue requirements.\n\nNow I'm setting up the project dependencies—React 18, React Router, Axios for API calls, and React Hot Toast for notifications. For styling, I'll keep it straightforward with a simple CSS file and inline styles rather than adding Tailwind complexity.\n\nWriting the project files...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":189,"cache_read_input_tokens":20732,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":189,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74582627-f9b4-4bf2-823b-05bb42d3c266","uuid":"bd498830-f3dc-47a1-bbee-bf41689da5d5"}
